  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of an 18th-Century Hammam in Guba</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The red brick masonry public bath house in Guba was the only public house in the area open to Muslim women during the late 18th and early 19th centuries. This project involves the conservation of the hammam in preparation for its eventual reuse as a cultural and tourism center.</narrative>
  </description>
